  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Women&apos;s leadership building, community organising and sustainable livelihoods</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Banteay Srei works with women and men in Cambodia with the aim of empowering vulnerable women to improve their political, economic and social situation.  Community development projects, together with advocacy and networking activities, are being implemented in 53 villages in Battambang and Siem Reap provinces.  Among the changes expected to be brought about are: more women in the target areas exercising their rights to participate in decentralisation processes and being elected as commune councillors; vulnerable families achieving improved livelihoods through the development of women&#x2019;s skills in sustainable agriculture, small business, disaster preparedness and natural resource management; and improved relationships between men and women (decreased violence against women, increased participation of women in social activities and increased shared household decision making).  This project aims to reach nearly 12,000 families (63,000 people).</narrative>
  </description>
